      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250319/assets/bfc628070a42e0c26d135fd100233ae0d13bfdcb5f327d294e2201d8e58ca6ee.png)\n\nWhat are the roots of the function $g(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $g(x)=0.$ In the given mapping diagram, we see that $g(5)=0$ and $g(9)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=5$ and $x=9.$",
