      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250319/assets/642d1393aa1e2d0c6303cafcf576eb2bcd007995d17beca8c65a740e3a61f125.png)\n\nWhat are the roots of the function $f(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given mapping diagram, we see that there is no value of $x$ that gives an output of zero. \n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has no roots.",
